(5247363, 758687, 68504, '<td valign="top">I find this exceptional in every way.  Pre-eminently it provokes our deepest emotional imagining, but it also challenges our preconceptions about visual representation.</td>', 'I find this exceptional in every way.  Pre-eminently it provokes our deepest emotional imagining, but it also challenges our preconceptions about visual representation.', '2009-02-09 16:04:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(5247372, 755178, 101059, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by paulbtlw:</b></div><hr/><i> Really interesting image - this is technically very intriguing; leaves me wondering what lens? was it software corrected? HDR? How many exposures? Was there a shift in focus between them to get an extended DOF?<br/> <br/>Or am I overcomplicating the shot - whatever, it''s a great result. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hi,<br/> <br/>Used a Sigma 10-20 lens with Nikon D300 on tripod.  Took 5 different exposures.  Used same aperture (F11) and bracketed 5 different raw images.  2 underexposed, 1 correct exposure, and 2 overexposures.  Then loaded these images into Photomatix (HDR). After that levels and some sharpening.  Thats it.  I know HDR is not to everyones taste, but i love it.<br/>Thanks for the nice comments.<br/>Owen</td>', 'Originally posted by paulbtlw: Really interesting image - this is technically very intriguing; leaves me wondering what lens? was it software corrected? HDR? How many exposures? Was there a shift in focus between them to get an extended DOF? Or am I overcomplicating the shot - whatever, it''s a great result.   Hi, Used a Sigma 10-20 lens with Nikon D300 on tripod.  Took 5 different exposures.  Used same aperture (F11) and bracketed 5 different raw images.  2 underexposed, 1 correct exposure, and 2 overexposures.  Then loaded these images into Photomatix (HDR). After that levels and some sharpening.  Thats it.  I know HDR is not to everyones taste, but i love it.Thanks for the nice comments.Owen', '2009-02-09 16:08:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(5247462, 760700, 30982, '<td valign="top">One could conceivably believe this is the same deer a year later.  Unlikely, sure, but still, one could believe it if one so desired!  I like both shots.  I like the head on inquisitive nature of the B&amp;W, I like the majesty of the pose of this one.</td>', 'One could conceivably believe this is the same deer a year later.  Unlikely, sure, but still, one could believe it if one so desired!  I like both shots.  I like the head on inquisitive nature of the B&W, I like the majesty of the pose of this one.', '2009-02-09 17:01:48.000000', NULL, 0),
