(5448544, 757049, 6519, '<td valign="top">Mighty powerful stuff there, Robert.<br/>The photo all by itself speaks volumes, and immediately "grabbed" me.<br/>The photo''s story adds even more impact.</td>', 'Mighty powerful stuff there, Robert.The photo all by itself speaks volumes, and immediately "grabbed" me.The photo''s story adds even more impact.', '2009-04-22 13:08:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(5448612, 757049, 42013, '<td valign="top">The dizzyness is what works. the brown hydrangeas, the empty chairs, and the bleakness of the ground make it powerful--of course knowing the entire back story makes it more so. thanks for sharing.</td>', 'The dizzyness is what works. the brown hydrangeas, the empty chairs, and the bleakness of the ground make it powerful--of course knowing the entire back story makes it more so. thanks for sharing.', '2009-04-22 13:47:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(5450106, 757049, 39427, '<td valign="top">Bear - The story behind this shot is somber and haunting, the coincidence is just crazy, and I am so sorry for your losses and especially their proximity to one another.  <br/> <br/>It is peculiar, indeed, how life can work out.  In my own shot of my father, it was literally the last picture on the memory card from the day and the last picture I ever took of him, and he died hunting in the same place where the photo was taken a month later.  I don''t know if it is the same for you, but the strangeness in the coincidences is somehow comforting, kinda makes me think about fate, though I admit I may just be searching for and pulling out meaning where none exists.<br/> <br/>In any case, I like your photograph, the dizziness, the mood, all that.  A great photo to be your ''most meaningful''.</td>', 'Bear - The story behind this shot is somber and haunting, the coincidence is just crazy, and I am so sorry for your losses and especially their proximity to one another.   It is peculiar, indeed, how life can work out.  In my own shot of my father, it was literally the last picture on the memory card from the day and the last picture I ever took of him, and he died hunting in the same place where the photo was taken a month later.  I don''t know if it is the same for you, but the strangeness in the coincidences is somehow comforting, kinda makes me think about fate, though I admit I may just be searching for and pulling out meaning where none exists. In any case, I like your photograph, the dizziness, the mood, all that.  A great photo to be your ''most meaningful''.', '2009-04-23 16:33:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(5453478, 760891, 97225, '<td valign="top">This is really lovely. The detail in the feathers and eye, the pose and the green background which sets the bird off so well - all beautiful.</td>', 'This is really lovely. The detail in the feathers and eye, the pose and the green background which sets the bird off so well - all beautiful.', '2009-04-27 03:32:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(5455141, 759904, 69008, '<td valign="top">I remember seeing this one in a challenge, and thinking "This looks like Silver Springs but it''s short on flowers".   The light on the columns adds a lot of interest, and the palm trunks repeating the vertical element of the columns is good too. <br/>The one leaning palm behind the left column sort of disturbs the vertical line of the column in some way, and at the same time, gives the edge of the column something solid in the B G to define it.  It''s a complex picture, and there are a lot of elements that seem to be not exactly working in unison to bring out a strong subject or make the viewer''s eye move through it to a subject. It''s a good scene to study.  The bright sky in the B G probably dinked the score pretty hard since it was in a F S challenge.</td>', 'I remember seeing this one in a challenge, and thinking "This looks like Silver Springs but it''s short on flowers".   The light on the columns adds a lot of interest, and the palm trunks repeating the vertical element of the columns is good too. The one leaning palm behind the left column sort of disturbs the vertical line of the column in some way, and at the same time, gives the edge of the column something solid in the B G to define it.  It''s a complex picture, and there are a lot of elements that seem to be not exactly working in unison to bring out a strong subject or make the viewer''s eye move through it to a subject. It''s a good scene to study.  The bright sky in the B G probably dinked the score pretty hard since it was in a F S challenge.', '2009-04-28 01:45:29.000000', NULL, 0),
